A||||40||cadero2dmax||Small Block Cad V8 conversions (excluding N*)||||14||
Z||000000||cadero2dmax||10-21-2001||08:47 AM||||I am just a little curious. How many others on this list have a  16 valve small block Cad (4.1 to 4.9) V8 sitting behind them?<P>There is a reason I ask. This is supposed to be a popular conversion, but all I have found is a lot of Fiero people that ask questions about my 4.9 conversion. Most are aware of the 4.6L Northstar swap, but few have seen or are aware of the other small block Caddy motors.<P>If you have a (non N*) Cad powered Fiero, speak up!!<P>------------------<BR>G<BR>Daily Driver - <BR>85 SE<BR>4.9 Cad<BR>Isuzu 5 speed<BR>'88 cradle<BR>lowered 2 1/2"<BR>Mr. Mikes interior<P>GRM $2002 Challenge Fiero<BR>84 coupe<BR>4.9 (carburated)<BR>2.86:1 TH-125 w/shift kit<p>[This message has been edited by cadero2dmax (edited 10-21-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||Philphine||10-21-2001||09:48 AM||||i guess you're aware of bubbajoe. he came through and got people hyped about it. i got some of his mounts myself. i think rockcrawl has done a few also. i've never heard it was popular. the ones that have done it all said it should be. guess it still has to catch on.||||reg||1
Z||000002||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-21-2001||09:48 AM||||how much work was it putting the 4.9 carbed in your 84?<P>I was thinking of putting a carbed v8 in mine.. <P>same boltup and stuff as the northstar?<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||cadero2dmax||10-21-2001||10:27 AM||||Not even close to a N* - - not nearly as difficult or expensive. There is a kit being developed that will make it almost a bolt in, including a plug-n-play harness so you can keep the injection.<P>For the carb, you can make (or buy) an adapter to fit your particular carb (I hope to use a Holley 500CFM 2 bbl such as those used by NASCAR for the Challenge car),modify the Cad distributor, plug the injector ports in the block - - DONE.<P>I will be chronicling my progress with the Challenge car on a list:<BR>GrassrootsChallengeFiero@yahoogroups.com<P>Included will be photos, text, discussion, and of course a lot of begging for parts :-)<P>G<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by isthiswhereiputausername?:<BR><B>how much work was it putting the 4.9 carbed in your 84?<P>I was thinking of putting a carbed v8 in mine.. <P>same boltup and stuff as the northstar?<P>Thanks</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||cadero2dmax||10-21-2001||10:39 AM||||I can only presume you haven't used BubbaJoe's mounts, or you would know they need modified to be used.<P>Your response is similar to those I have received in other forums. It seems everybody knows of somebody with a Cad conversion - but with the exception of Team Python and Ed Parks, I can't find anybody else with a Cad motor behind them.<P>BubbaJoe's "list" consists of a couple people actually trying to do this swap, but mostly wannabe's. <P>Thus my search for others that actually have a 4.1 to 4.9 non-Northstar engine (running) in their Fiero.<P>I don't think they exist!!<P>G<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B>i guess you're aware of bubbajoe. he came through and got people hyped about it. i got some of his mounts myself. i think rockcrawl has done a few also. i've never heard it was popular. the ones that have done it all said it should be. guess it still has to catch on.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||10-21-2001||12:35 PM||||Hello!, <BR> Hey cadero2dmax, don't let everyone know how cheap and easy these swaps are! Can't it be our own little secret? Seriously though, I drove my Cadero yesterday. I'm running a '90 port injected 4.5. I have two more PFI 4.5s and two 4.9s lined up here waiting to be put into Fieros. I've spoken with Lance Mullen in CA, he had just finished a 4.9 swap in his kitcar when he got called out for military service. He is also running the port injection and a 5 speed. Team Python is also running the PFI with a 5 speed. I've spoken to them a few times (via email) and from what I gathered they are running in limp mode. JimmyB up in Canada is putting a car together with a '89 TBI 4.5. Those are the only ones I know of besides the little bit I've heard about Ed Parks developing a kit. IMO this swap is too easy to warrant a kit. I'm working on a new front mount so that I don't need to modify the cradle on every car I do. I've seen bubbajoe's mount and I don't like it.<P>My site: <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/cadero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/cadero.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||cadero2dmax||10-21-2001||02:28 PM||||Well, it is probably the easiest engine swap (except for the 3.1/3.4 V6) that there is. I thought the Quad 4 conversion was easy!!<P>But there are some distinct advantages to Ed's kit. First, to custom machine a billet flywheel would probably cost as much as the whole kit Ed offers. Then there is the "plug-n-play" harness, no need to pin-out the wiring ( a long and tedious task, as you must well know). The mounts fit (unlike BubbaJoe's stuff), and without letting any of his secrets out of the bag, let's just say the poly engine mounts are sweet. ;-)<P>Would you consider a Cadero list (for owners or builders, no "wannabe's)? How about some of the other parties you mentioned? We could compare notes, such as the aforementioned poly mounts. Or the status of the 5.7 SFI computer mating that is being undertaken - so that all the SBC chips and re-calibration tricks can be used? Or maybe the cam re-timing tricks? Oh, I guess I need to add etc!<P>Lemme No<P>G <P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B>Hello!, <BR> Hey cadero2dmax, don't let everyone know how cheap and easy these swaps are! Can't it be our own little secret? Seriously though, I drove my Cadero yesterday. I'm running a '90 port injected 4.5. I have two more PFI 4.5s and two 4.9s lined up here waiting to be put into Fieros. I've spoken with Lance Mullen in CA, he had just finished a 4.9 swap in his kitcar when he got called out for military service. He is also running the port injection and a 5 speed. Team Python is also running the PFI with a 5 speed. I've spoken to them a few times (via email) and from what I gathered they are running in limp mode. JimmyB up in Canada is putting a car together with a '89 TBI 4.5. Those are the only ones I know of besides the little bit I've heard about Ed Parks developing a kit. IMO this swap is too easy to warrant a kit. I'm working on a new front mount so that I don't need to modify the cradle on every car I do. I've seen bubbajoe's mount and I don't like it.<P>My site: <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/cadero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/cadero.htm</A> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||12
Z||000007||rockcrawl||10-21-2001||03:34 PM||||Well I just typed up a nice long reply and then accidently deleted it before posting. so in summary, Yes, I think we need a Cadero list for those of us who are neck deep in Caderos to share info.||||reg||1
Z||000008||cadero2dmax||10-21-2001||05:31 PM||||DONE!<P>Although I wanted it to read a little different, there is a Cadero Owners Forum at the following URL: caderoOwnersForum@yahoogroups.com<P>Membership is by invitation, or at least must be approved. I have set it so any moderators must approve same, and will e-mail all applications from potential members prior to approval.<P>Jump on in if you have a Cadero.<P>G||||reg||1
