Z||000011||Daleford||10-22-2001||07:56 AM||||Just noticed this thread.  What great timing. I just sat in my stretched Fiero yesterday, turned the key , and listened to my 4.9 purr for the first time. This chassis is for a Koenig Testarossa, 7 foot 3 inch wide body so I used the complete Caddy drivetrain with cradle, to increase track width.<BR>Not crazy about the narrow Fiero transaxel. Also not crazy about spending $2000 on adapter kits, plus a Northstar/SB Chev/ whatever after that. This complete 4.9 V-8   4 speed automatic, computer, cradle, wiring, everything cost $500! Sure, I had to adapt the Caddy mounts to the Fiero chassis and my mechanic had to read from a Caddy and a Fiero manual at the same time to do the wiring, but hey,,, we are hotrodders!<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000012||MinnGreenGT||10-22-2001||09:52 AM||||I'd certainly be interested in getting more info on this "kit" you speak of!  I've got a "dead" '84SE that I'd love to ressurect with a Caddy V8- I don't have much of a problem with the physical installation... I'm just not a fan of the wiring thing.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
